  "published": "2026-10-23T13:50:57.813Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.0: security and reliability improvements. Upgrade by bumping the package version; no code changes are required.\n- If your site runs behind a proxy or CDN, configure ASP.NET Core forwarded headers with your proxy's addresses so client IPs are correct, and set RazorKitOptions.AllowedOrigins to your public URL.\n- MapRazorKit() is optional: if your site already calls MapControllers() and MapRazorPages(), you don't need it.\n- axe-core is now bundled with the package; a CSP no longer needs to allow unpkg.com for RazorKit.\n- The public constructors of RazorKit's controller, page model and services take additional parameters (affects only code that constructs them directly).\n- When two stories share a name, the first one now wins.\n- Rate-limit rejection logs identify clients by a short per-process tag, not by IP address.\n- The preview's invalid-JSON message is now a fixed message; details are shown only in Development.\n- Live editing in the Controls panel needs HTTPS, or localhost.\n- If your site has its own Pages/RazorKit.cshtml (for example from an in-repo copy of RazorKit), delete it: it overrides the package's page.",
